==Trivia==
* There are two identical "Accurate" combat styles on powered staves. This is because prior to [[Update:6th Birthday and QoL|an update]] on [[21 February]] [[2019]], the game did not remember the selected combat style of the previous weapon equipped, and would attempt to move selection to the same position where the style was located. For example, having the "Rapid" style on a bow and switching to a spear would result in it being on the "Swipe" style.
** This proved to be an inconvenience when switching between a powered staff and another weapon, which would often force the staff into the "Longrange" style due to it being in the same position as the "Rapid" style on ranged weapons, and forcing ranged weapons to the "Accurate" style if players switched back to the "Accurate" style on a powered staff. Forgetting to switch the styles back to "Accurate" on a powered staff would result in gaining [[Defence]] experience (due to being on the "Longrange" style) which some players, especially [[One-defence pure|one-defence pures]], did not wish to gain.
** This was remedied in [[Update:New Animations & Barbarian Assault Changes|an update]] on [[24 September]] [[2015]] by giving powered staves a second identical "Accurate" style to prevent it from switching the combat style for other weapons. However, this was made obsolete with the update that gave the game the ability to remember active combat styles for different types of weapons.

